IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1 -- Part 6 Chapter 2 and Chapter 3 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and
-- Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United Kingdom:
-- regs 53 to 60B (lines 1789-2054 of uksi-2017-692.txt).  The text is a plain-text rendering
-- made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against
-- the official text.
--
-- WHAT THESE REGULATIONS DO.  They set up the registers the FCA and the Commissioners keep of
-- the businesses that must be registered before they trade (money service businesses, trust or
-- company service providers, high value dealers, cryptoasset businesses and others), say what an
-- applicant must give, when the registering authority must refuse, may refuse, and may suspend
-- or cancel, and what notices follow; reg 60A makes a cryptoasset business tell its customer when
-- the Ombudsman and the Compensation Scheme do not cover it.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.  NOTHING is "the
-- Regulations do not answer on these facts" and is never read as no.  A duty "must" that has not
-- been discharged, a flat negative, a "provided that", "if", "where", "when" or "upon" that
-- fails, and a case outside a period the text fixes in its own words, answer JUST FALSE and carry
-- FALSE-kind with the words that say no (rulings of 2026-11-05); a scope limit with no "only"
-- (a relative clause, a class of persons), a list that is not closed and an answer that belongs to
-- another section answer NOTHING and carry NOTHING-kind with the reason.  Where a function named
-- for the permitted act cannot say that an unmet condition leaves a prohibition off, a twin named
-- for the prohibition ("the prohibition ... applies") carries that answer (fork F10).  Marginal
-- readings (a), (b) and (c) are in NOTES.md.
-- A fact a witness can state is a plain input.  An answer that belongs to another section or to
-- the keel is an input named for the section it comes from (a SEAM, PLAN.md section 5).
-- Counting.  "within 28 days beginning with the day of X" counts the day of X as day 1, so the
-- last day is X plus 27; "within 28 days of X" has the last day X plus 28 (marginal reading (d),
-- NOTES.md).

§ `Part 6 Chapter 2 -- Registration (regs 53 to 60)`

-- Every act a registering authority is asked to do, and every act a person is asked to do or not
-- to do, by Chapters 2 and 3, named for its provision, for the regulative form of each duty.
DECLARE `reg 53 act of a registering authority` IS ONE OF
    `reg 54(1) maintain a register of the relevant persons the paragraph names`
    `reg 54(1A) maintain a register of cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers`
    `reg 54(2) maintain a register of the relevant persons the paragraph names`
    `reg 55(4) take reasonable steps to bring the decision to maintain a register to the attention of the relevant persons`
    `reg 57(3) decide whether to require further information`
    `reg 58(1) refuse to register an applicant who is not fit and proper`
    `reg 58A(1) refuse to register a cryptoasset business that is not fit and proper`
    `reg 59(2) give the applicant notice of the decision`
    `reg 59(3) give the applicant notice of the decision or that it is minded not to register`
    `reg 59(4) decide and give the applicant notice`
    `reg 59(5) include the person in the register`
    `reg 59(7) publish the status of the appeal and its outcome`
    `reg 60(6) inform the registering authority of grounds for suspension or cancellation`
    `reg 60(7) give the person notice of the decision to suspend or cancel`
    `reg 60(8) give the person notice that it is minded to suspend or cancel`
    `reg 60(9) decide and give the person notice`
    `reg 60(12) publish the status of the appeal and its outcome`

DECLARE `reg 56 act of a person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 56(1) act as a business that must be registered`
    `reg 56(5) carry on the business or profession for more than twelve months without registration`
    `reg 56(6)(b) carry on the business or profession on or after 10th June 2021 without registration`
    `reg 56B(1) inform the FCA that the firm intends to act or has begun to act`
    `reg 56B(3) inform the FCA that the firm has ceased to act`
    `reg 56B(4) provide the FCA with details of a change or a correction`
    `reg 57(4) provide the registering authority with details of a change or a correction`
    `reg 60A(2) inform the customer`

§§ `Regulation 53 -- Interpretation`

-- The authority that registers a person: the FCA for those it must register under reg 54(1) or
-- (1A) and those it decides to register under reg 55(1); the Commissioners for those they must
-- register under reg 54(2) and those they decide to register under reg 55(3).  The four facts
-- are the answers of regs 54 and 55 to the person; each section answers on its own (E1) and the
-- seat hands the four to this function.
-- src:1792 | “registering authority” means—
-- src:1793 | the FCA, in relation to—
-- src:1794 | those relevant persons which it is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A); and
-- src:1795 | those relevant persons it decides to register under regulation 55(1);
-- src:1796 | the Commissioners, in relation to—
-- src:1797 | those relevant persons which they are required to register under regulation 54(2); and
-- src:1798 | those relevant persons they decide to register under regulation 55(3);
@ref reg 53 “registering authority” (src:1792-1798)
GIVEN `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
`reg 53 the registering authority for the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` OR `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)`
    THEN JUST `the Financial Conduct Authority`
    ELSE IF `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` OR `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)`
         THEN JUST `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition names the registering authority only "in relation to" the four classes it lists; for any other person the Chapter names no registering authority
         ELSE NOTHING

-- The same definition as a yes/no question about a given authority.  "Registering authority means"
-- a closed list of two heads, so an authority that is neither head of this person is not the
-- registering authority (JUST FALSE), as is any other body.
@ref reg 53 “registering authority” (src:1792-1798)
GIVEN `the authority` IS AN Authority
      `the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 53 the authority is the registering authority for the person` MEANS
    IF (`the authority` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority` AND (`the person is one the FCA is required to register under regulation 54(1) or (1A)` OR `the FCA has decided to register the person under regulation 55(1)`))
       OR (`the authority` EQUALS `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` AND (`the person is one the Commissioners are required to register under regulation 54(2)` OR `the Commissioners have decided to register the person under regulation 55(3)`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registering authority” means— the FCA, in relation to ...; the Commissioners, in relation to ..." -- a definition handed to a closed list of two heads (delegated reading (a) of 2026-11-05), and neither head holds
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1799 | “telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider” means an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions where the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of any telecommunication, digital or IT device and the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services (and terms used in this definition which are defined in the Payment Services Regulations 2017 have the meanings given in those Regulations).
@ref reg 53 “telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider” (src:1799)
GIVEN `it is an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of a telecommunication, digital or IT device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 53 the undertaking is a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` MEANS
    IF `it is an undertaking which provides payment services consisting of the execution of payment transactions`
       AND `the consent of the payer to execute a payment transaction is given by means of a telecommunication, digital or IT device`
       AND `the payment is made to the telecommunication, IT system or network operator acting only as an intermediary between the payment service user and the supplier of the goods and services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an undertaking which" -- one of the three conditions is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 54 -- Duty to maintain registers of certain relevant persons`

-- The facts about a person that regs 54 and 55 sort on.  Each is a plain fact the registering
-- authority can state, except the notification under reg 23, which is reg 23's answer (SEAM S-9).
DECLARE `reg 54 registrant` HAS
    `an authorised person`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `reg 23 the person has notified the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a cryptoasset exchange provider`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `a custodian wallet provider`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `an authorised cryptoasset firm`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a specified investment cryptoasset firm`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a high value dealer`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a money service business`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trust or company service provider`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bill payment service provider for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN

-- SEAM S-9 (asking): the notification is reg 23's fact.
-- src:1801 | (1) The FCA must maintain a register of those relevant persons who—
-- src:1802 | (a) are authorised persons, and
-- src:1803 | (b) have notified the FCA under regulation 23 that they are acting, or intend to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider.
@ref reg 54(1) (src:1801-1803)
GIVEN person IS A `reg 54 registrant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(1) the person is one the FCA must register` MEANS
    IF person's `an authorised person`
       AND person's `reg 23 the person has notified the FCA that it is acting, or intends to act, as a money service business or a trust or company service provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must maintain a register of those relevant persons who (a) are authorised persons, and (b) have notified" -- a person outside the two limbs is outside the duty, and the paragraph does not say it may not be registered
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 54(1) (src:1801)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 54(1) the FCA must maintain the register (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 54(1) maintain a register of the relevant persons the paragraph names`

-- Reg 54(1A) is printed twice.  The first printing (lines 1804-1806) requires a register of
-- cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers; the second (lines 1807-1813)
-- limits it to those that are not authorised cryptoasset firms or specified investment
-- cryptoasset firms.  Both are in the text and the text does not say which replaces which, so
-- each is encoded on its own (fork F1) and the seat asks the second as the later printing.
-- src:1804 | (1A) The FCA must maintain a register of—
-- src:1805 | (a) cryptoasset exchange providers; and
-- src:1806 | (b) custodian wallet providers.
@ref reg 54(1A) first printing (src:1804-1806)
GIVEN person IS A `reg 54 registrant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(1A) the person is one the FCA must register (first printing)` MEANS
    IF person's `a cryptoasset exchange provider` OR person's `a custodian wallet provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must maintain a register of (a) cryptoasset exchange providers; and (b) custodian wallet providers" -- another person is outside the duty
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1807 | (1A) The FCA must maintain a register of those relevant persons who—
-- src:1808 | (a) are—
-- src:1809 | (i) cryptoasset exchange providers, or
-- src:1810 | (ii) custodian wallet providers, but
-- src:1811 | (b) are not—
-- src:1812 | (i) authorised cryptoasset firms, or
-- src:1813 | (ii) specified investment cryptoasset firms.
@ref reg 54(1A) second printing (src:1807-1813)
GIVEN person IS A `reg 54 registrant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(1A) the person is one the FCA must register (second printing)` MEANS
    IF (person's `a cryptoasset exchange provider` OR person's `a custodian wallet provider`)
       AND (NOT person's `an authorised cryptoasset firm`)
       AND (NOT person's `a specified investment cryptoasset firm`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must maintain a register of those relevant persons who (a) are ... but (b) are not" -- an authorised cryptoasset firm, a specified investment cryptoasset firm or another person is outside the duty
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1804 | (1A) The FCA must maintain a register of—
@ref reg 54(1A) (src:1804)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 54(1A) the FCA must maintain the register (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 54(1A) maintain a register of cryptoasset exchange providers and custodian wallet providers`

-- "who are not included in the register maintained by the FCA under paragraph (1) and are (a)
-- high value dealers; (b) money service businesses; (c) trust or company service providers; (d)
-- bill payment service providers, for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority; (e)
-- telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers, for which the Commissioners are
-- the supervisory authority".  Whether the person is in the FCA's register is a second fact.
-- src:1814 | (2) The Commissioners must maintain a register of those relevant persons who are not included in the register maintained by the FCA under paragraph (1) and are—
-- src:1815 | (a) high value dealers;
-- src:1816 | (b) money service businesses;
-- src:1817 | (c) trust or company service providers;
-- src:1818 | (d) bill payment service providers, for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority;
-- src:1819 | (e) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers, for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority.
@ref reg 54(2) (src:1814-1819)
GIVEN person IS A `reg 54 registrant`
      `the person is included in the register maintained by the FCA under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(2) the person is one the Commissioners must register` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is included in the register maintained by the FCA under paragraph (1)`)
       AND (person's `a high value dealer`
            OR person's `a money service business`
            OR person's `a trust or company service provider`
            OR person's `a bill payment service provider for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority`
            OR person's `a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider for which the Commissioners are the supervisory authority`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must maintain a register of those relevant persons who are not included in the register maintained by the FCA ... and are (a) to (e)" -- a person already in the FCA's register, or of another description, is outside the duty
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 54(2) (src:1814)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 54(2) the Commissioners must maintain the register (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 54(2) maintain a register of the relevant persons the paragraph names`

-- "(3) Subject to paragraph (4) the registering authorities may keep the registers required by
-- this regulation in any form they think fit."  Paragraph (4) binds the Commissioners' register
-- only; the proviso fails when that register lacks the entries.
-- src:1820 | (3) Subject to paragraph (4) the registering authorities may keep the registers required by this regulation in any form they think fit.
-- src:1821 | (4) The register maintained by the Commissioners must include entries in the registers maintained under regulation 25 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked.
@ref reg 54(3) (src:1820-1821)
GIVEN `the register is the one maintained by the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register includes the entries paragraph (4) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(3) the registering authority may keep the register in the form it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the register is the one maintained by the Commissioners` AND (NOT `the register includes the entries paragraph (4) requires`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (4)" -- a proviso that is not met (Marginal readings, (a))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1821 | (4) The register maintained by the Commissioners must include entries in the registers maintained under regulation 25 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked.
@ref reg 54(4) (src:1821)
GIVEN `the register includes entries in the registers maintained under regulation 25 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(4) the register maintained by the Commissioners includes the entries the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the register includes entries in the registers maintained under regulation 25 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1822 | (5) A registering authority may publish or make available to public inspection all or part of a register maintained by it under this regulation.
@ref reg 54(5) (src:1822)
GIVEN `it is a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 54(5) the registering authority may publish or make available to public inspection all or part of the register` MEANS
    IF `it is a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register maintained by it under this regulation" -- another register is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 55 -- Power to maintain registers`

-- SEAM S-10 (asking): whether the person falls within reg 10(2)(a) is reg 10's answer.
-- src:1825 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), an “Annex 1 financial institution” is a financial institution which—
-- src:1826 | (a) falls within regulation 10(2)(a), and
-- src:1827 | (b) is not—
-- src:1828 | (i) a money service business;
-- src:1829 | (ii) an authorised person;
-- src:1830 | (iii) a bill payment service provider; or
-- src:1831 | (iv) a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider.
@ref reg 55(2) (src:1825-1831)
GIVEN `reg 10(2)(a) the person falls within regulation 10(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a bill payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(2) the person is an Annex 1 financial institution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a financial institution`)
       OR `the person is a money service business`
       OR `the person is an authorised person`
       OR `the person is a bill payment service provider`
       OR `the person is a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a financial institution which ... is not (i) a money service business; (ii) an authorised person; (iii) a bill payment service provider; or (iv) a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider" -- the definition is closed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 10(2)(a) the person falls within regulation 10(2)(a)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which (a) falls within regulation 10(2)(a)" -- the person does not
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person falls within reg 10(2)(a) is that regulation's answer and it has not been given
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1824 | (1) The FCA may maintain a register of Annex 1 financial institutions.
@ref reg 55(1) (src:1824)
GIVEN `the register is a register of Annex 1 financial institutions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(1) the FCA may maintain the register` MEANS
    IF `the register is a register of Annex 1 financial institutions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may maintain a register of Annex 1 financial institutions" -- a register of other persons is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `reg 55(3) description of relevant person` IS ONE OF
    `reg 55(3)(a) estate agents`
    `reg 55(3)(b) auditors`
    `reg 55(3)(c) external accountants`
    `reg 55(3)(d) tax advisers`
    `reg 55(3)(e) bill payment service providers`
    `reg 55(3)(f) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers`
    `reg 55(3)(g) letting agents`
    `reg 55(3)(h) art market participants`
    `reg 55(3) any other description`

-- The rendering shows "..." after (e): text was removed there.
-- src:1832 | (3) The Commissioners may maintain registers of relevant persons who are not supervised by any of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1, and who are—
-- src:1833 | (a) estate agents,
-- src:1834 | (b) auditors;
-- src:1835 | (c) external accountants;
-- src:1836 | (d) tax advisers;
-- src:1837 | (e) bill payment service providers; ...
-- src:1838 | (f) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service providers;
-- src:1839 | (g) letting agents; or
-- src:1840 | (h) art market participants.
@ref reg 55(3) (src:1832-1840)
GIVEN description IS A `reg 55(3) description of relevant person`
      `the person is supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(3) the Commissioners may maintain a register of the relevant persons` MEANS
    IF `the person is supervised by one of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relevant persons who are not supervised by any of the professional bodies listed in Schedule 1" -- a person so supervised is outside the permission
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER description
         WHEN `reg 55(3) any other description` THEN NOTHING
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who are (a) estate agents ... (h) art market participants" -- a person of another description is outside the permission
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1841 | (4) Where a registering authority decides to maintain a register under this regulation, it must take reasonable steps to bring its decision to the attention of those relevant persons in respect of which the register is to be established.
@ref reg 55(4) (src:1841)
GIVEN `the registering authority has decided to maintain a register under regulation 55` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken reasonable steps to bring its decision to the attention of the relevant persons in respect of which the register is to be established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(4) the registering authority has taken reasonable steps to bring its decision to the attention of the relevant persons` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registering authority has decided to maintain a register under regulation 55`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a registering authority decides to maintain a register under this regulation" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it has taken reasonable steps to bring its decision to the attention of the relevant persons in respect of which the register is to be established`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take reasonable steps" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 55(4) (src:1841)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 55(4) the registering authority must take reasonable steps to bring its decision to the attention of the relevant persons (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 55(4) take reasonable steps to bring the decision to maintain a register to the attention of the relevant persons`

-- src:1842 | (5) Subject to paragraph (6) a registering authority may maintain a register under this regulation in any form it thinks fit.
-- src:1843 | (6) The registers maintained by the registering authorities must include entries in any equivalent registers maintained under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked.
@ref reg 55(5) (src:1842-1843)
GIVEN `the register includes the entries paragraph (6) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(5) the registering authority may maintain the register in any form it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the register includes the entries paragraph (6) requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (6)" -- a proviso that is not met (Marginal readings, (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1843 | (6) The registers maintained by the registering authorities must include entries in any equivalent registers maintained under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked.
@ref reg 55(6) (src:1843)
GIVEN `the register includes entries in any equivalent registers maintained under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(6) the registers maintained by the registering authorities include the entries the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the register includes entries in any equivalent registers maintained under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 which were current immediately before the date that regulation was revoked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include" (Marginal readings, (c))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1844 | (7) A registering authority may publish or make available to public inspection all or part of a register maintained by it under this regulation.
@ref reg 55(7) (src:1844)
GIVEN `it is a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 55` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 55(7) the registering authority may publish or make available to public inspection all or part of the register` MEANS
    IF `it is a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 55`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a register maintained by it under this regulation" -- another register is outside the permission
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 56 -- Requirement to be registered`

-- The prohibition of reg 56(1), named for the act it permits.  JUST FALSE where it bites (ruling
-- N2).  When an exception applies the paragraph does not say the person may act, so NOTHING.
-- The two exceptions are facts here: the seat passes paragraph (2) and reg 56A as "shown to apply"
-- (their functions answer NOTHING when they are not shown to), which is marginal reading (e).
-- src:1846 | (1) Unless a person in respect of whom the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 is included in the appropriate register, or paragraph (2) or regulation 56A (transitional provision for existing cryptoasset businesses) applies, that person must not act as a—
-- src:1847 | (a) high value dealer;
-- src:1848 | (b) money service business;
-- src:1849 | (c) trust or company service provider;
-- src:1850 | (d) bill payment service provider; ...
-- src:1851 | (e) telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider;
-- src:1852 | (f) cryptoasset exchange provider; or
-- src:1853 | (g) custodian wallet provider.
@ref reg 56(1) (src:1846-1853)
GIVEN `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is included in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 56A applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(1) the person may act as the business` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person`)
       OR (NOT `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person in respect of whom the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 ... must not act as a (a) to (g)" -- another person or another business is outside the prohibition
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the appropriate register` OR `paragraph (2) applies to the person` OR `regulation 56A applies to the person`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the prohibition is lifted by "Unless", and the paragraph does not say that the person may act
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that person must not act as a"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The prohibition of reg 56(1) asked in its own polarity: does it apply to the person?  "Unless" is
-- "if not": when the person is on the register, or paragraph (2) or regulation 56A applies, the
-- prohibition does not apply and the answer is JUST FALSE (fork F10).
@ref reg 56(1) (src:1846-1853)
GIVEN `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is included in the appropriate register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 56A applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(1) the prohibition on acting as the business applies to the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 in respect of the person`)
       OR (NOT `the person acts as a high value dealer, a money service business, a trust or company service provider, a bill payment service provider, a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider, a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person in respect of whom the registering authorities are required to maintain a register under regulation 54 ... must not act as a (a) to (g)" -- another person or another business is outside the prohibition
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the appropriate register` OR `paragraph (2) applies to the person` OR `regulation 56A applies to the person`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a person ... is included in the appropriate register, or paragraph (2) or regulation 56A applies" -- the exception holds, so the prohibition does not apply (fork F10)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref reg 56(1) (src:1846)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56(1) the person shall not act as a business that must be registered (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 56(1) act as a business that must be registered`

-- src:1854 | (2) This paragraph applies if—
-- src:1855 | (a) the person concerned is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider, or a telecommunications, digital and IT payment service provider and has applied for registration in the register but that application has not yet been determined; or
-- src:1856 | (b) the person concerned is a money service business or a trust or company service provider and has, before 10th January 2020, applied for registration in the register but that application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 56(2) (src:1854-1856)
GIVEN `the person is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for registration in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
      `the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(2) paragraph (2) applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has applied for registration in the register` AND `the application has not yet been determined`
       AND (`the person is a high value dealer, a bill payment service provider or a telecommunication, digital and IT payment service provider`
            OR (`the person is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` AND (Day `the date of the application`) LESS THAN (Day (Date 10 1 2020))))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies if (a) ... or (b) ..." -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); neither limb holds
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Reg 56(3): a person registered under reg 25 or 32 of the 2007 Regulations is treated as
-- included in the new register, (a) for the 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came
-- into force (26 June 2017, so 26 June 2017 to 25 June 2018), and (b) after that period if the
-- additional information was given within it.
-- src:1857 | (3) A relevant person which is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 is to be treated as included in the appropriate registers maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 54 or 55 of these Regulations for the purpose of paragraph (1)—
-- src:1858 | (a) during the period of 12 months beginning with the date on which these Regulations come into force, and
-- src:1859 | (b) after that period, if the person concerned has provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period referred to in sub-paragraph (a).
@ref reg 56(3) (src:1857-1859)
GIVEN `the person is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the person provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(3) the person is treated as included in the appropriate register on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person which is registered in the register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) LESS THAN (Day `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force`)
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Regulations were not yet in force on that day and the paragraph does not speak to it
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) LESS THAN (Day (`add months` `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force` 12))
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `the person provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the day the Regulations came into force`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) after that period, if the person concerned has provided the additional information" -- the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1860 | (4) A relevant person which is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007 is to be treated as included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 55(1) for the purposes of paragraph (1).
@ref reg 56(4) (src:1860)
GIVEN `the person is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(4) the person is treated as included in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 55(1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A relevant person which is registered in the register maintained by the FCA under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Reg 56(5).  The prohibition is on carrying on for MORE than 12 months, so it bites from the day
-- 12 months after the register is established (or the amendment comes into force).  Inside the
-- twelve months the paragraph does not forbid and does not say the person may.
-- src:1861 | (5) Where a registering authority decides to maintain a register under regulation 55(1) or (3) in respect of any description of relevant persons and establishes a register for that purpose, or where a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations, a relevant person of that description must not carry on the business or profession in question for a period of more than 12 months beginning with the date on which the registering authority establishes the register or (as the case may be) the date on which the amendment comes into force unless—
-- src:1862 | (a) that person is included in the register, ...
-- src:1863 | (b) that person has applied for registration in the register, but that application has not yet been determined, or
-- src:1864 | (c) that person is an art market participant or a letting agent.
@ref reg 56(5) (src:1861-1864)
GIVEN `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(5) the relevant person may carry on the business or profession on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a registering authority decides to maintain a register under regulation 55(1) or (3) ... and establishes a register" -- the "where" is unmet, so the prohibition is not triggered; this function is named for the permitted act, so JUST FALSE would say the opposite of the text (marginal reading (f), fork F6; twin in fork F10)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the register`
            OR `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined`
            OR `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the prohibition is lifted by "unless" and the paragraph does not say that the person may carry on
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) AT LEAST (Day (`add months` `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` 12))
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not carry on the business or profession in question for a period of more than 12 months beginning with the date"
              THEN JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind (silent): inside the twelve months the paragraph does not forbid, and does not say that the person may
              ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition of reg 56(5) asked in its own polarity: does it apply on the day?  JUST FALSE
-- where the "where" is unmet (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)), where an exception holds, and inside the
-- twelve months (outside the period of the prohibition); JUST TRUE after them (fork F6, fork F10).
@ref reg 56(5) (src:1861-1864)
GIVEN `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(5) the prohibition on carrying on the business or profession applies to the relevant person on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a registering authority has established a register under regulation 55(1) or (3), or a new description of relevant persons is required to be registered in consequence of an amendment to these Regulations`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a registering authority decides to maintain a register under regulation 55(1) or (3) ... and establishes a register" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); the prohibition is not triggered
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the register`
            OR `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined`
            OR `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (a) that person is included in the register, (b) that person has applied ... or (c) ... an art market participant or a letting agent" -- the exception holds, so the prohibition does not apply (fork F10)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) AT LEAST (Day (`add months` `the date on which the register is established or the amendment comes into force` 12))
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of more than 12 months beginning with the date" -- the day is inside the twelve months, outside the period of the prohibition (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
              ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 56(5) (src:1861)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56(5) the relevant person shall not carry on the business or profession for more than twelve months (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 56(5) carry on the business or profession for more than twelve months without registration`

-- Reg 56(6)(a): an art market participant or letting agent must apply before 10 June 2021.
-- Reg 56(6)(b): and must not carry on on or after that date unless registered or pending.
-- src:1865 | (6) An art market participant or a letting agent—
-- src:1866 | (a) must apply for registration in the register before 10th June 2021;
@ref reg 56(6)(a) (src:1865-1866)
GIVEN `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person applied for registration` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(6)(a) the person has applied for registration before 10th June 2021` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An art market participant or a letting agent" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date the person applied for registration`
         WHEN JUST applied THEN
             IF (Day applied) LESS THAN (Day (Date 10 6 2021))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must apply for registration in the register before 10th June 2021" -- the application came on or after that day
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF (Day `the day in question`) LESS THAN (Day (Date 10 6 2021))
             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person has not yet applied and the day for applying has not yet passed
             THEN NOTHING
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must apply for registration in the register before 10th June 2021" -- no application by that day
             ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1867 | (b) must not carry on that business or profession on or after 10th June 2021 unless—
-- src:1868 | (i) that person is included in the register, or
-- src:1869 | (ii) that person has applied for registration in the register, but the application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 56(6)(b) (src:1867-1869)
GIVEN `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(6)(b) the person may carry on the business or profession on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An art market participant or a letting agent" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the register` OR `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the prohibition is lifted by "unless" and the paragraph does not say that the person may carry on
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) AT LEAST (Day (Date 10 6 2021))
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not carry on that business or profession on or after 10th June 2021"
              THEN JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind (silent): before that day the paragraph does not forbid, and does not say that the person may
              ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition of reg 56(6)(b) asked in its own polarity: does it apply on the day?  It runs "on
-- or after 10th June 2021", so before that day it does not apply, and it does not apply to a person
-- on the register or with an application pending (fork F10).
@ref reg 56(6)(b) (src:1867-1869)
GIVEN `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is included in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56(6)(b) the prohibition on carrying on applies to the art market participant or letting agent on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an art market participant or a letting agent`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An art market participant or a letting agent" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person is included in the register` OR `the person has applied for registration in the register and the application has not yet been determined`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (i) that person is included in the register, or (ii) that person has applied" -- the exception holds, so the prohibition does not apply (fork F10)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF (Day `the day in question`) AT LEAST (Day (Date 10 6 2021))
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or after 10th June 2021" -- the day is before the prohibition begins, outside its period (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
              ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 56(6)(b) (src:1867)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56(6)(b) the art market participant or letting agent shall not carry on on or after 10th June 2021 (as a prohibition)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    SHANT `reg 56(6)(b) carry on the business or profession on or after 10th June 2021 without registration`

§§ `Regulation 56A -- Transitional provision for existing cryptoasset businesses: requirement to register`

-- src:1879 | (2) In this regulation, “existing cryptoasset exchange provider” and “existing custodian wallet provider” mean a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider which was carrying on business as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider (as the case may be) in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020.
@ref reg 56A(2) (src:1879)
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was carrying on business as such in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56A(2) the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` MEANS
    IF `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` AND `it was carrying on business as such in the United Kingdom immediately before 10th January 2020`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mean a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider which was carrying on business ... immediately before 10th January 2020"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The earlier of two possible days, either of which may not have occurred.
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE DATE
      second IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`reg 56A(1) the earlier of two possible days` MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN NOTHING THEN second
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
        WHEN JUST b THEN IF (Day a) AT MOST (Day b) THEN JUST a ELSE JUST b

-- "Regulation 56 does not apply to an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing
-- custodian wallet provider until" the first of (a), (b) and (c).  "Until" fixes the end, so the
-- answer on a later day is JUST FALSE (a bar encoded as its own yes/no question: JUST TRUE before
-- the end, JUST FALSE from it; the answer never says that regulation 56 applies).
-- src:1871 | (1) Regulation 56 does not apply to an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider until—
-- src:1872 | (a) the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA;
-- src:1873 | (b) where the FCA gives the person notice under regulation 59(4)(b) of the FCA’s decision not to register that person—
-- src:1874 | (i) the date on which the FCA states that the decision takes effect, or
-- src:1875 | (ii) if the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect, the date on which the FCA gives a notice to the person which includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it; or
-- src:1876 | (c) 10th January 2021 if before that date neither of the following has occurred—
-- src:1877 | (i) the giving of notice to that person by the FCA under regulation 59(3);
-- src:1878 | (ii) the expiry of the period specified in regulation 59(3A) for the FCA to give such notice.
@ref reg 56A(1) (src:1871-1878)
GIVEN `the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `before 10th January 2021 the FCA gave the person notice under regulation 59(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before 10th January 2021 the period specified in regulation 59(3A) expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56A(1) regulation 56 does not apply to the existing cryptoasset business on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an existing cryptoasset exchange provider or existing custodian wallet provider" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        LET `the end by decision` MEANS
                IF `the FCA considers that the interests of the public require its decision to have immediate effect`
                THEN `the date the FCA gave a notice including a statement to that effect and the reasons for it`
                ELSE `the date the decision not to register takes effect, as the FCA states it, where the FCA gave notice under regulation 59(4)(b)`
            `the end by default` MEANS
                IF (NOT `before 10th January 2021 the FCA gave the person notice under regulation 59(3)`) AND (NOT `before 10th January 2021 the period specified in regulation 59(3A) expired`)
                THEN JUST (Date 10 1 2021)
                ELSE NOTHING
            `the end` MEANS `reg 56A(1) the earlier of two possible days` (`reg 56A(1) the earlier of two possible days` `the date the person is included in the register maintained under regulation 54(1A) following the determination of its application by the FCA` `the end by decision`) `the end by default`
        IN CONSIDER `the end`
           -- none of (a), (b) and (c) has fixed an end, so the regulation continues not to apply: the bar is still in force (delegated reading (d) of 2026-11-05); the answer never says that regulation 56 applies
           WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
           WHEN JUST e THEN
               IF (Day `the day in question`) LESS THAN (Day e)
               THEN JUST TRUE
               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply ... until" -- the day is on or after the end
               ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 56B -- Requirement that cryptoasset firms acting as cryptoasset exchange providers or custodian wallet providers inform the FCA`

-- "before acting ... or within 28 days of so doing": last day is the day it began plus 28.
-- src:1881 | (1) An authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm must, before acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA that it intends, or has begun, to act as such.
@ref reg 56B(1) (src:1881)
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the firm began to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A DATE
      `the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(1) the firm has informed the FCA before acting or within 28 days of so doing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the firm informed the FCA`
         WHEN JUST informed THEN
             IF (Day informed) AT MOST ((Day `the day the firm began to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider`) PLUS 28)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before acting ... or within 28 days of so doing, inform the FCA" -- informed later than 28 days after it began
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN ((Day `the day the firm began to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider`) PLUS 28)
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... inform the FCA" -- 28 days have passed and it has not informed
             THEN JUST FALSE
             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): it has not yet informed the FCA and the 28 days have not yet passed
             ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 56B(1) (src:1881)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56B(1) the firm must inform the FCA (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 56B(1) inform the FCA that the firm intends to act or has begun to act`

-- The exemption: acting immediately before the full commencement day and continuing after it, and
-- informing the FCA within the 30 days beginning with that day.  The text does not give the full
-- commencement day: it names a regulation of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000
-- (Cryptoassets) Regulations 2026 that the rendering does not reproduce (fork F4), so the day is
-- an input.
-- src:1882 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm which—
-- src:1883 | (a) immediately before the date specified by regulation 1(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Cryptoassets) Regulations 2026 (citation, commencement and extent) (“the full commencement day”) was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date, and
-- src:1884 | (b) informs the FCA that it is acting as such within 30 days beginning with the full commencement day.
@ref reg 56B(2) (src:1882-1884)
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the full commencement day the firm was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the full commencement day` IS A DATE
      `the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the firm` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm`)
       OR (NOT `immediately before the full commencement day the firm was acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider and continues to act as such after that date`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm which (a) ... was acting ... and continues to act" -- another firm is outside the exemption
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the firm informed the FCA that it is acting as such`
         WHEN JUST informed THEN
             IF (Day informed) AT LEAST (Day `the full commencement day`) AND (Day informed) AT MOST ((Day `the full commencement day`) PLUS 29)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) informs the FCA that it is acting as such within 30 days beginning with the full commencement day" -- the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN ((Day `the full commencement day`) PLUS 29)
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) informs the FCA ... within 30 days beginning with the full commencement day" -- the 30 days have passed with no notice
             THEN JUST FALSE
             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): it has not yet informed the FCA and the 30 days have not yet passed
             ELSE NOTHING

-- The period "N days beginning with" a day: the day itself is day 1, so the last day is the day
-- plus N minus 1.  An act done before the period begins is outside it, so the answer is JUST FALSE
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F11).
GIVEN `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the length of the period in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the act was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the act was done`
    WHEN JUST done THEN
        IF (Day done) LESS THAN (Day `the day the period begins`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within N days beginning with" -- the act was done before the period began, outside it (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F11)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF (Day done) AT MOST ((Day `the day the period begins`) PLUS (`the length of the period in days` MINUS 1))
             THEN JUST TRUE
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within N days beginning with" -- the act was done after the last day
             ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN ((Day `the day the period begins`) PLUS (`the length of the period in days` MINUS 1))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within N days beginning with" -- the period has passed and the act has not been done
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the act has not been done and the period has not yet passed
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1885 | (3) Where an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm ceases to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider, it must inform the FCA within 28 days beginning with the day of ceasing to act as such.
@ref reg 56B(3) (src:1885)
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of ceasing` IS A DATE
      `the day the firm informed the FCA` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(3) the firm has informed the FCA within 28 days beginning with the day of ceasing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `the firm ceased to act as a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... ceases to act" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` `the day of ceasing` 28 `the day the firm informed the FCA` `the day in question`

@ref reg 56B(3) (src:1885)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56B(3) the firm must inform the FCA that it has ceased to act (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 56B(3) inform the FCA that the firm has ceased to act`

-- src:1886 | (4) If, at any time after an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm (“A”) has provided the FCA with any information under this regulation—
-- src:1887 | (a) there is a material change affecting any matter contained in that information, or
-- src:1888 | (b) it becomes apparent to A that the information contains an inaccuracy,
-- src:1889 | then A must provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy within 30 days beginning with the date of the change or the discovery of the inaccuracy.
@ref reg 56B(4) (src:1886-1889)
GIVEN `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has provided the FCA with information under regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the firm that the information contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE
      `the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(4) the firm has provided the FCA with details of the change or a correction within 30 days beginning with the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the firm is an authorised cryptoasset firm or a specified investment cryptoasset firm`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an authorised cryptoasset firm or specified investment cryptoasset firm (A)" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it has provided the FCA with information under regulation 56B`)
            OR (NOT `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the firm that the information contains an inaccuracy`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, at any time after [the firm] has provided the FCA with any information under this regulation (a) there is a material change ... or (b) it becomes apparent ... inaccuracy" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` 30 `the day the firm provided details of the change or a correction` `the day in question`

@ref reg 56B(4) (src:1886)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 56B(4) the firm must provide the FCA with details of the change or a correction (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 56B(4) provide the FCA with details of a change or a correction`

-- src:1890 | (5) Any information provided to the FCA under this regulation must be in such form and verified in such manner as the FCA may specify.
@ref reg 56B(5) (src:1890)
GIVEN `the information was provided to the FCA under regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the form specified by the FCA and verified in the manner the FCA specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(5) the information is in the form and verified in the manner the FCA may specify` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information was provided to the FCA under regulation 56B`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any information provided to the FCA under this regulation" -- other information is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is in the form specified by the FCA and verified in the manner the FCA specified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and verified in such manner as the FCA may specify" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1891 | (6) Any requirement imposed by this regulation is to be treated as if it were a requirement imposed by or under FSMA.
@ref reg 56B(6) (src:1891)
GIVEN `it is a requirement imposed by regulation 56B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 56B(6) the requirement is to be treated as if it were a requirement imposed by or under FSMA` MEANS
    IF `it is a requirement imposed by regulation 56B`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any requirement imposed by this regulation" -- another requirement is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 57 -- Applications for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55`

-- src:1893 | (1) A person applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 (“an applicant”) must make an application in such manner and provide such information as the registering authority may specify.
@ref reg 57(1) (src:1893)
GIVEN `the person is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant made the application in the manner, and provided the information, that the registering authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(1) the applicant has made the application in the manner and provided the information the registering authority may specify` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55" -- another person is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the applicant made the application in the manner, and provided the information, that the registering authority specified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must make an application in such manner and provide such information as the registering authority may specify" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (2): the items the registering authority may specify.  The list is not closed ("includes,
-- among other things"), so an item not in it answers NOTHING.  Items (b), (h), (i) and (j) are
-- limited to certain applicants.
DECLARE `reg 57(2) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `reg 57(2)(a) the applicant's full name and where different the name of the business`
    `reg 57(2)(b) where the applicant is an individual, the applicant's date of birth and residential address`
    `reg 57(2)(c) the nature of the business`
    `reg 57(2)(d) the address of the head office of the business with its company number, and of any branches in the United Kingdom`
    `reg 57(2)(e) the full name of the nominated officer`
    `reg 57(2)(f) a risk assessment which satisfies the requirements in regulation 18`
    `reg 57(2)(g) information as to the way in which the business meets the requirements of these Regulations, Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000, Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 and Part 8 of that Act`
    `reg 57(2)(h)(i) the full name, date of birth and residential address of any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the business or service provider`
    `reg 57(2)(h)(ii) information needed to decide whether it must refuse the application pursuant to regulation 58`
    `reg 57(2)(i) the full name and address of any agent the money service business uses`
    `reg 57(2)(j)(i) the name of the applicant's supervisory authority`
    `reg 57(2)(j)(ii) confirmation from the applicant's supervisory authority that any person mentioned in regulation 58(1) is a fit and proper person`
    `reg 57(2)(k) whether the applicant, or any person named in the application, has been convicted of a criminal offence listed in Schedule 3`
    `reg 57(2) any other item`

-- src:1894 | (2) The information which the registering authority may specify includes, among other things—
-- src:1895 | (a) the applicant's full name and where different the name of the business;
-- src:1896 | (b) where the applicant is an individual, the applicant's date of birth and residential address;
-- src:1897 | (c) the nature of the business;
-- src:1898 | (d) the address of the head office of the business with its company number (in the case of a company), and of any branches the business has in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1899 | (e) the full name of the nominated officer (if any);
-- src:1900 | (f) a risk assessment which satisfies the requirements in regulation 18;
-- src:1901 | (g) information as to the way in which the business meets the requirements set out in—
-- src:1902 | (i) these Regulations;
-- src:1903 | (ii) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 (terrorist property) ;
-- src:1904 | (iii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (money laundering) ; and
-- src:1905 | (iv) Part 8 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (investigations);
-- src:1906 | (h) in relation to a money service business or a trust or company service provider—
-- src:1907 | (i) the full name, date of birth and residential address of any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the business or service provider; and
-- src:1908 | (ii) information needed by the registering authority to decide whether it must refuse the application pursuant to regulation 58;
-- src:1909 | (i) in relation to a money service business, the full name and address of any agent it uses for the purposes of its business;
-- src:1910 | (j) where the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant—
-- src:1911 | (i) the name of the applicant's supervisory authority;
-- src:1912 | (ii) confirmation from the applicant's supervisory authority that any person mentioned in regulation 58(1) is a fit and proper person within the meaning of that regulation;
-- src:1913 | (k) whether the applicant, or any person named in the application, has been convicted of a criminal offence listed in Schedule 3.
@ref reg 57(2) (src:1894-1913)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 57(2) item of information`
      `the applicant is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(2) the registering authority may specify the item of information` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(b) where the applicant is an individual, the applicant's date of birth and residential address` THEN
        IF `the applicant is an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the applicant is an individual" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(h)(i) the full name, date of birth and residential address of any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the business or service provider` THEN
        IF `the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) in relation to a money service business or a trust or company service provider" -- for another applicant the paragraph does not say
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(h)(ii) information needed to decide whether it must refuse the application pursuant to regulation 58` THEN
        IF `the applicant is a money service business or a trust or company service provider` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) in relation to a money service business or a trust or company service provider" -- for another applicant the paragraph does not say
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(i) the full name and address of any agent the money service business uses` THEN
        IF `the applicant is a money service business` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) in relation to a money service business" -- for another applicant the paragraph does not say
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(j)(i) the name of the applicant's supervisory authority` THEN
        IF `the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(j) where the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `reg 57(2)(j)(ii) confirmation from the applicant's supervisory authority that any person mentioned in regulation 58(1) is a fit and proper person` THEN
        IF `the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(j) where the registering authority is not the supervisory authority for the applicant" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "includes, among other things" -- an item not listed is neither allowed nor forbidden by the paragraph
    WHEN `reg 57(2) any other item` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1914 | (3) At any time after receiving an application and before determining it, the registering authority may require the applicant to provide, within 21 days beginning with the date on which the requirement is issued, such further information as the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application.
@ref reg 57(3) (src:1914)
GIVEN `the registering authority has received the application and has not yet determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is what the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(3) the registering authority may require the applicant to provide further information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registering authority has received the application and has not yet determined it`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At any time after receiving an application and before determining it" -- outside that window (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the information is what the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such further information as the registering authority reasonably considers necessary to enable it to determine the application" -- other information is outside the permission and the paragraph does not forbid it
         ELSE NOTHING

@ref reg 57(3) (src:1914)
GIVEN `the day the requirement is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the applicant provided the information` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(3) the applicant has provided the further information within 21 days beginning with the date on which the requirement is issued` MEANS
    `reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` `the day the requirement is issued` 21 `the day the applicant provided the information` `the day in question`

-- src:1915 | (4) Without prejudice to the application of regulation 60B, if at any time after the applicant has provided the registering authority with any information under paragraph (1) or (3) (whether before or after the applicant is registered)—
-- src:1916 | (a) there is a material change affecting any matter contained in that information; or
-- src:1917 | (b) it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy,
-- src:1918 | the applicant must provide the registering authority with details of the change or a correction of the inaccuracy within 30 days beginning with the date of the occurrence of the change (or the discovery of the inaccuracy) or within such later time as may be agreed with the registering authority.
@ref reg 57(4) (src:1915-1918)
GIVEN `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE
      `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(4) the applicant has provided the registering authority with details of the change or a correction in time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)`)
       OR (NOT `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if at any time after the applicant has provided the registering authority with any information ... there is a material change ... or it becomes apparent ... inaccuracy" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` 30 `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` `the day in question`
         WHEN JUST later THEN
             CONSIDER `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction`
             WHEN JUST done THEN
                 IF (Day done) LESS THAN (Day `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy`)
                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days beginning with the date of the change" -- the details were given before the change, outside the period (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F11)
                 THEN JUST FALSE
                 ELSE IF (Day done) AT MOST (Day later) THEN JUST TRUE
                      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days beginning with the date ... or within such later time as may be agreed" -- after the agreed later time
                      ELSE JUST FALSE
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN (Day later)
                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within such later time as may be agreed" -- the agreed time has passed with nothing provided
                 THEN JUST FALSE
                 -- NOTHING-kind (silent): nothing provided yet and the agreed time has not yet passed
                 ELSE NOTHING

-- "(whether before or after the applicant is registered)": whether the applicant has been registered
-- makes no difference, so this twin takes it as an input and gives the same answer for either value.
@ref reg 57(4) (src:1915-1918)
GIVEN `the applicant has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` IS A DATE
      `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(4) whether before or after registration, the applicant has provided the registering authority with details of the change or a correction in time` MEANS
    `reg 57(4) the applicant has provided the registering authority with details of the change or a correction in time` `the applicant has provided the registering authority with information under paragraph (1) or (3)` `there is a material change affecting a matter contained in that information, or it becomes apparent to the applicant that the information contains an inaccuracy` `the day of the change or of the discovery of the inaccuracy` `a later time has been agreed with the registering authority` `the day the applicant provided details of the change or a correction` `the day in question`

@ref reg 57(4) (src:1915)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 57(4) the applicant must provide the registering authority with details of the change or a correction (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 57(4) provide the registering authority with details of a change or a correction`

-- src:1919 | (5) The obligation in paragraph (4) applies also to material changes or inaccuracies affecting any matter contained in any supplementary information provided pursuant to that paragraph.
@ref reg 57(5) (src:1919)
GIVEN `the change or inaccuracy affects a matter contained in supplementary information provided pursuant to paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(5) the obligation in paragraph (4) applies to the change or inaccuracy` MEANS
    IF `the change or inaccuracy affects a matter contained in supplementary information provided pursuant to paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies also to material changes or inaccuracies affecting any matter contained in any supplementary information provided pursuant to that paragraph" -- other changes are dealt with by paragraph (4) itself
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1920 | (6) Any information to be provided to the registering authority under this regulation must be in such form and verified in such manner as the authority may specify.
@ref reg 57(6) (src:1920)
GIVEN `the information is to be provided to the registering authority under regulation 57` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the form specified by the registering authority and verified in the manner it specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 57(6) the information is in the form and verified in the manner the registering authority may specify` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the information is to be provided to the registering authority under regulation 57`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any information to be provided to the registering authority under this regulation" -- other information is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it is in the form specified by the registering authority and verified in the manner it specified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and verified in such manner as the authority may specify" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 58 -- Fit and proper test`

-- SEAM S-K2 (asking): who is a beneficial owner of the applicant is the keel's answer (regs 5
-- and 6).  The function passes that answer on to the question whether the registering authority
-- must count the person among those whose fitness it examines.
-- src:1925 | (c) a beneficial owner of the applicant; or
@ref reg 58(1)(c) (src:1925)
-- SEAM S-K2 (asking)
GIVEN `reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 58(1)(c) the person is a beneficial owner of the applicant whose fitness the registering authority must consider` MEANS
    `reg 5 and 6 the individual is a beneficial owner of the customer`

-- src:1922 | (1) The registering authority must refuse to register an applicant for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider, if it is satisfied that—
-- src:1923 | (a) the applicant;
-- src:1924 | (b) an officer or manager of the applicant;
-- src:1925 | (c) a beneficial owner of the applicant; or
-- src:1926 | (d) where the applicant is a money service business—
-- src:1927 | (i) any agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business; or
-- src:1928 | (ii) any officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent,
-- src:1929 | is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business.
@ref reg 58(1) (src:1922-1929)
GIVEN `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a money service business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is satisfied that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is satisfied that an officer or manager of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is satisfied that a beneficial owner of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is satisfied that an agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business, or an officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent, is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 58(1) the registering authority must refuse to register the applicant` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the applicant is applying for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an applicant for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 as a money service business or as a trust or company service provider" -- another applicant is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the registering authority is satisfied that the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business`
            OR `the registering authority is satisfied that an officer or manager of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business`
            OR `the registering authority is satisfied that a beneficial owner of the applicant is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business`
            OR (`the applicant is a money service business` AND `the registering authority is satisfied that an agent used by the applicant for the purposes of its business, or an officer, manager or beneficial owner of the agent, is not a fit and proper person to carry on that business`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must refuse to register an applicant ... if it is satisfied that" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 58(1) (src:1922)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 58(1) the registering authority must refuse to register (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 58(1) refuse to register an applicant who is not fit and proper`

