§§ `Regulation 59 -- Determination of applications for registration under regulations 54 and 55`

-- src:1951 | (1) Subject to regulation 58 and regulation 58A, the registering authority may refuse to register an applicant for registration in a register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 if—
-- src:1952 | (a) any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with;
-- src:1953 | (b) it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular;
-- src:1954 | (c) the applicant has failed to pay—
-- src:1955 | (i) a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9;
-- src:1956 | (ii) a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11; or
-- src:1957 | (iii) a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007;
-- src:1958 | (d) where the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority, the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds; or
-- src:1959 | (e) the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds—
-- src:1960 | (i) that the applicant will fail to comply with any of its obligations under—
-- src:1961 | (aa) these Regulations;
-- src:1962 | (bb) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ; or
-- src:1963 | (cc) Parts 7 and 8 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ;
-- src:1964 | (the “relevant obligations”);
-- src:1965 | (ii) that any person whom the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations.
@ref reg 59(1) (src:1951-1965)
GIVEN `any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has failed to pay a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9, a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11, or a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the applicant, or a person the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers, will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(1) the registering authority may refuse to register the applicant` MEANS
    IF `any requirement of, or imposed under, regulation 57 has not been complied with`
       OR `it appears to the registering authority that any information provided pursuant to regulation 57 is false or misleading in a material particular`
       OR `the applicant has failed to pay a penalty imposed by the authority under Part 9, a charge imposed by the authority under Part 11, or a penalty or charge imposed by the authority under regulation 35(1) or 42(1) of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`
       OR (`the registering authority is not the applicant's supervisory authority` AND `the supervisory authority opposes the application for registration on reasonable grounds`)
       OR `the registering authority suspects, on reasonable grounds, that the applicant, or a person the applicant has identified as one of its officers or managers, will fail to comply with any of the relevant obligations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may refuse to register an applicant ... if" -- none of (a) to (e) is met; an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-19 (answering): regs 93 and 99 ask which decisions can be appealed.
@ref reg 59(1) (src:1951)
GIVEN `the decision is to refuse to register an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 59(1) the decision refuses to register an applicant` MEANS `the decision is to refuse to register an applicant`

-- Reg 59(2).  The 45 days run from the day the Commissioners receive the application or, where
-- they required further information under regulation 57(3), the day they receive it (fork F7).
-- src:1966 | (2) Where the Commissioners are the registering authority, they must within 45 days beginning either with the date on which they receive the application or, where applicable, with the date on which they receive any further information required under regulation 57(3), give the applicant notice of—
@ref reg 59(2) (src:1966)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Commissioners received the application` IS A DATE
      `the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(2) the Commissioners have given the applicant notice within 45 days` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioners are the registering authority`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioners are the registering authority" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        LET `the day the 45 days begin` MEANS
                CONSIDER `the day the Commissioners received the further information required under regulation 57(3)`
                WHEN JUST further THEN further
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the Commissioners received the application`
        IN `reg 56B(3) the act was done within the days beginning with the starting day` `the day the 45 days begin` 45 `the day the Commissioners gave the applicant notice` `the day in question`

@ref reg 59(2) (src:1966)
GIVEN `the notice states the decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for the decision, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(2) the Commissioners' notice states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the decision to register the applicant` OR `the notice states the decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for the decision, the right to a review under regulation 94 and the right to appeal under regulation 99`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "give the applicant notice of (a) the decision to register the applicant; or (b) the following matters" -- the notice states neither
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 59(2) (src:1966)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 59(2) the Commissioners must give the applicant notice (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 59(2) give the applicant notice of the decision`

-- Reg 59(3) and (3A).  The period is 3 months for a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian
-- wallet provider and 45 days otherwise, beginning on the day the FCA receives the application
-- or the further information (fork F7).  "3 months beginning with" a day ends the day before the
-- same day three months on.
-- src:1979 | (3A) The period specified in this paragraph is—
-- src:1980 | (i) where the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider, 3 months, or
-- src:1981 | (ii) in any other case, 45 days,
-- src:1982 | beginning either with the date on which it receives the application or, where applicable, with the date on which it receives any further information required under regulation 57(3).
@ref reg 59(3A) (src:1979-1982)
GIVEN `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the 3 months or 45 days begin` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 59(3A) the last day of the period specified in this paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider`
    THEN Date ((Day (`add months` `the day the 3 months or 45 days begin` 3)) MINUS 1)
    ELSE Date ((Day `the day the 3 months or 45 days begin`) PLUS 44)

-- src:1973 | (3) Where the FCA is the registering authority, it must within the period specified in paragraph (3A), give the applicant notice of—
@ref reg 59(3) (src:1973)
GIVEN `the FCA is the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the FCA received the application` IS A DATE
      `the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the FCA gave the applicant notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(3) the FCA has given the applicant notice within the period specified in paragraph (3A)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the FCA is the registering authority`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the FCA is the registering authority" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE
        LET `the day the period begins` MEANS
                CONSIDER `the day the FCA received the further information required under regulation 57(3)`
                WHEN JUST further THEN further
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the FCA received the application`
            `the last day` MEANS `reg 59(3A) the last day of the period specified in this paragraph` `the applicant is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` `the day the period begins`
        IN CONSIDER `the day the FCA gave the applicant notice`
           WHEN JUST given THEN
               IF (Day given) LESS THAN (Day `the day the period begins`)
               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period specified in paragraph (3A)" -- notice was given before the period began, outside it (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F11)
               THEN JUST FALSE
               ELSE IF (Day given) AT MOST (Day `the last day`)
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within the period specified in paragraph (3A), give the applicant notice" -- notice came after the last day
                    ELSE JUST FALSE
           WHEN NOTHING THEN
               IF (Day `the day in question`) GREATER THAN (Day `the last day`)
               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within the period specified in paragraph (3A), give the applicant notice" -- the period has passed with no notice
               THEN JUST FALSE
               -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no notice yet and the period has not yet passed
               ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1973 | (3) Where the FCA is the registering authority, it must within the period specified in paragraph (3A), give the applicant notice of—
-- src:1974 | (a) its decision to register the applicant; or
-- src:1975 | (b) the following matters—
-- src:1976 | (i) that it is minded not to register the applicant;
-- src:1977 | (ii) the reasons for being minded to refuse to register the applicant; and
-- src:1978 | (iii) the right to make representations to it within a specified period (which may not be less than 28 days).
@ref reg 59(3) (src:1973-1978)
GIVEN `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that it is minded not to register the applicant, the reasons for being minded to refuse, and the right to make representations to it within a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period specified for representations, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(3) the FCA's notice states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states its decision to register the applicant`
       OR (`the notice states that it is minded not to register the applicant, the reasons for being minded to refuse, and the right to make representations to it within a specified period`
           AND `the period specified for representations, in days` AT LEAST 28)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "give the applicant notice of (a) its decision to register the applicant; or (b) the following matters" -- the notice states neither, or the period for representations is under 28 days
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 59(3) (src:1973)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 59(3) the FCA must give the applicant notice (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 59(3) give the applicant notice of the decision or that it is minded not to register`

-- src:1983 | (4) After the expiry of the period referred to in paragraph (3)(b)(iii), the FCA must decide, within a reasonable period, whether to register the applicant and it must give the applicant notice of—
-- src:1984 | (a) its decision to register the applicant; or
-- src:1985 | (b) the following matters—
-- src:1986 | (i) its decision not to register the applicant;
-- src:1987 | (ii) the reasons for its decision; and
-- src:1988 | (iii) the right to appeal under regulation 93.
@ref reg 59(4) (src:1983-1988)
GIVEN `the period for representations has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states its decision to register the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states its decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for its decision, and the right to appeal under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(4) the FCA has decided and given the applicant notice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the period for representations has expired`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the expiry of the period referred to in paragraph (3)(b)(iii)" -- the period has not expired; a fixed period outside which the text says no (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the FCA decided within a reasonable period`
            AND (`the notice states its decision to register the applicant` OR `the notice states its decision not to register the applicant, the reasons for its decision, and the right to appeal under regulation 93`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must decide, within a reasonable period, whether to register the applicant and it must give the applicant notice of" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 59(4) (src:1983)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 59(4) the FCA must decide and give the applicant notice (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 59(4) decide and give the applicant notice`

-- src:1989 | (5) The registering authority must, as soon as practicable after deciding to register a person, include that person in the relevant register.
@ref reg 59(5) (src:1989)
GIVEN `the registering authority has decided to register the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(5) the registering authority has included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registering authority has decided to register the person`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after deciding to register a person" -- the condition is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it included the person in the relevant register as soon as practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, as soon as practicable ..., include that person in the relevant register" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 59(5) (src:1989)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 59(5) the registering authority must include the person in the register (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 59(5) include the person in the register`

-- src:1990 | (6) Where—
-- src:1991 | (a) the registering authority decides not to register an applicant, the authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information about that decision as the authority considers appropriate;
@ref reg 59(6)(a) (src:1990-1991)
GIVEN `the registering authority decides not to register an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(6)(a) the registering authority may publish information about its decision not to register` MEANS
    IF `the registering authority decides not to register an applicant` AND `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the registering authority decides not to register an applicant, the authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish" -- an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1990 | (6) Where—
-- src:1992 | (b) the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B (changes in control of registered cryptoasset businesses) from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business and the FCA decides to object to the acquisition, the FCA may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information about that decision as the FCA considers appropriate.
@ref reg 59(6)(b) (src:1990-1992)
GIVEN `the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA decides to object to the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(6)(b) the FCA may publish information about its decision to object to the acquisition` MEANS
    IF `the FCA has received a notice under Part 12 of FSMA as modified by regulation 60B and Schedule 6B from a person who decides to acquire or increase control over a registered cryptoasset business`
       AND `the FCA decides to object to the acquisition`
       AND `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... the FCA may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish" -- an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1993 | (7) Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (6) and the person whose registration is refused, or whose acquisition is the subject of objection, refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal, the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish information about the status of the appeal and its outcome in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (6).
@ref reg 59(7) (src:1993)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person whose registration is refused, or whose acquisition is the subject of objection, refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay, in the same manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(7) the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (6)`) OR (NOT `the person whose registration is refused, or whose acquisition is the subject of objection, refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (6) and the person ... refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay, in the same manner`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, without delay, publish" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 59(7) (src:1993)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 59(7) the supervisory authority must publish the status of the appeal (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 59(7) publish the status of the appeal and its outcome`

-- src:1994 | (8) In this regulation, “registered cryptoasset business” means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider which is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A).
@ref reg 59(8) (src:1994)
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59(8) the person is a registered cryptoasset business` MEANS
    IF `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` AND `it is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider which is included in a register maintained by the FCA under regulation 54(1A)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 60 -- Cancellation and suspension of registration in a register under regulation 54 or 55`

-- Reg 60(1) and (2).  The five routes to suspension or cancellation are given by separate
-- paragraphs (1)+(2), (2A), (3), (4) and (5); each is answered on its own (ruling E1) and the
-- function `reg 60 the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` gathers them
-- by hand at the end of the regulation.
-- src:1996 | (1) If paragraph (2) applies, the registering authority may suspend (for such period as it considers appropriate) or cancel—
-- src:1997 | (a) the registration of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54; or
-- src:1998 | (b) the registration of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55 (including the registration of an Annex 1 financial institution previously included in a register maintained under regulation 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007) .
-- src:1999 | (2) This paragraph applies if, at any time after registration, the registering authority is satisfied that—
-- src:2000 | (a) the money service business, trust or company service provider, or Annex 1 financial institution (as the case may be); or
-- src:2001 | (b) any other person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to that business, provider, or financial institution,
-- src:2002 | is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58.
@ref reg 60(1) (src:1996-2002)
GIVEN `the registration is of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54, or of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to it, is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(1) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registration is of a money service business or a trust or company service provider in a register maintained under regulation 54, or of an Annex 1 financial institution in a register maintained under regulation 55`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the registration of (a) a money service business or a trust or company service provider ... (b) an Annex 1 financial institution" -- another registration is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the registering authority is satisfied that the registered person, or another person mentioned in regulation 58(1) in relation to it, is not a fit and proper person for the purposes of regulation 58`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If paragraph (2) applies, the registering authority may suspend or cancel" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2003 | (2A) The FCA may suspend (for such period as it considers appropriate) or cancel the registration of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider if, at any time after registration, the FCA is satisfied that the cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider (as the case may be) does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2).
@ref reg 60(2A) (src:2003)
GIVEN `the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA is satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(2A) the FCA may suspend or cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registration is of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the registration of a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider" -- another registration is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the FCA is satisfied that the registered person does not meet the requirement in regulation 58A(2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, at any time after registration, the FCA is satisfied that" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- SEAM S-12 (asking): whether the person failed to comply with a notice under reg 66 is a fact
-- that regulation's answer supplies.
-- src:2004 | (3) The registering authority may suspend (for such period as it considers appropriate) or cancel a person's registration in a register maintained by it under regulation 54 or 55 if, at any time after registration—
-- src:2005 | (a) it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply; or
-- src:2006 | (b) the person has failed to comply with any requirement of a notice given under regulation 66.
@ref reg 60(3) (src:2004-2006)
-- SEAM S-12 (asking)
GIVEN `the registration is in a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(3) the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registration is in a register maintained by the registering authority under regulation 54 or 55`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person's registration in a register maintained by it under regulation 54 or 55" -- another registration is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it appears to the authority that any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of regulation 59(1) apply` OR `reg 66 the person has failed to comply with a requirement of a notice given under regulation 66`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, at any time after registration (a) it appears ... or (b) the person has failed to comply" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2007 | (4) The Commissioners may suspend (for such period as they consider appropriate) or cancel the registration of a person who—
-- src:2008 | (a) was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007, and
-- src:2009 | (b) has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date on which these Regulations come into force.
@ref reg 60(4) (src:2007-2009)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date these Regulations came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(4) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioners are the registering authority`
       AND `the person was included in a register maintained by the Commissioners under regulation 25 or 32 of the Money Laundering Regulations 2007`
       AND `the person has not provided the additional information required for registration under regulation 57 within the period of 12 months beginning with the date these Regulations came into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration of a person who (a) was included in a register ... and (b) has not provided" -- a person outside (a) and (b) is outside the paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2010 | (5) The Commissioners may suspend (for such period as they consider appropriate) or cancel the registration of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b) where the money service business is—
-- src:2011 | (a) providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so;
-- src:2012 | (b) not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Service Regulations 2017; and
-- src:2013 | (c) not a person—
-- src:2014 | (i) mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a “payment service provider” in regulation 2(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017, or
-- src:2015 | (ii) to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies.
@ref reg 60(5) (src:2010-2015)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration is of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money service business is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or a person to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(5) the Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioners are the registering authority`) OR (NOT `the registration is of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commissioners may suspend or cancel the registration of a money service business in a register maintained under regulation 54(2)(b)" -- another registrant or authority is outside the paragraph
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the money service business is providing a payment service in the United Kingdom, or is purporting to do so`
            AND `it is not included in the register of payment service providers maintained by the FCA under regulation 4(1) of the Payment Services Regulations 2017`
            AND (NOT `it is a person mentioned in paragraphs (d) to (j) of the definition of a payment service provider in regulation 2(1) of those Regulations, or a person to whom regulation 3 or 154(2) of those Regulations applies`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the money service business is (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Hand-gathered (ruling E1, option B as guidance): the five routes give one legal effect, a
-- power to suspend or cancel.  JUST TRUE if any route gives it; JUST FALSE only if every route
-- answers no; otherwise NOTHING.  Each route stays answerable on its own above.
GIVEN `the answer of regulation 60(1) and (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 60(2A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 60(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 60(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of regulation 60(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60 the registering authority may suspend or cancel the registration by any route` MEANS
    IF `the answer of regulation 60(1) and (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of regulation 60(2A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of regulation 60(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of regulation 60(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of regulation 60(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the answer of regulation 60(1) and (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `the answer of regulation 60(2A)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `the answer of regulation 60(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `the answer of regulation 60(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            AND `the answer of regulation 60(5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every route that speaks to the registration answers no
         THEN JUST FALSE
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a route is outside its scope, or has not been answered, and no route gives the power
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2016 | (6) Where the supervisory authority of a person on the register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 is not the registering authority, the supervisory authority must inform the registering authority as soon as possible if it becomes aware of any grounds on which the registering authority might decide to suspend or cancel that person's registration.
@ref reg 60(6) (src:2016)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority of a person on the register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 is not the registering authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has become aware of grounds on which the registering authority might decide to suspend or cancel the registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it informed the registering authority as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(6) the supervisory authority has informed the registering authority as soon as possible` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the supervisory authority of a person on the register maintained under regulation 54 or 55 is not the registering authority`)
       OR (NOT `the supervisory authority has become aware of grounds on which the registering authority might decide to suspend or cancel the registration`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the supervisory authority ... is not the registering authority, the supervisory authority must inform ... if it becomes aware" -- an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it informed the registering authority as soon as possible`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must inform the registering authority as soon as possible" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60(6) (src:2016)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 60(6) the supervisory authority must inform the registering authority (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 60(6) inform the registering authority of grounds for suspension or cancellation`

-- src:2017 | (7) Where the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration they must give that person notice of—
-- src:2018 | (a) their decision and, subject to paragraph (10), the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect;
-- src:2019 | (b) if appropriate, the period of the suspension;
-- src:2020 | (c) the reasons for their decision;
-- src:2021 | (d) the right to a review under regulation 94; and
-- src:2022 | (e) the right to appeal under regulation 99.
@ref reg 60(7) (src:2017-2022)
GIVEN `the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the decision and the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a period of suspension is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to a review under regulation 94` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 99` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(7) the Commissioners' notice states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the notice states the decision and the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect`
            AND ((NOT `a period of suspension is appropriate`) OR `the notice states the period of the suspension`)
            AND `the notice states the reasons for the decision`
            AND `the notice states the right to a review under regulation 94`
            AND `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 99`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they must give that person notice of (a) ... (e)" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60(7) (src:2017)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 60(7) the Commissioners must give the person notice (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 60(7) give the person notice of the decision to suspend or cancel`

-- src:2023 | (8) Where the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration it must give that person notice—
-- src:2024 | (a) that it is so minded;
-- src:2025 | (b) if appropriate, the proposed period of the suspension;
-- src:2026 | (c) the reasons for being so minded; and
-- src:2027 | (d) the right to make representations to it within the period specified in the notice (which must not be less than 28 days).
@ref reg 60(8) (src:2023-2027)
GIVEN `the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that it is so minded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a period of suspension is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the proposed period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the reasons for being so minded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to make representations within the period specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period specified for representations, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(8) the FCA's notice states what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the FCA is minded to suspend or cancel a person's registration" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the notice states that it is so minded`
            AND ((NOT `a period of suspension is appropriate`) OR `the notice states the proposed period of the suspension`)
            AND `the notice states the reasons for being so minded`
            AND `the notice states the right to make representations within the period specified in the notice`
            AND `the period specified for representations, in days` AT LEAST 28
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must give that person notice (a) ... (d) ... (which must not be less than 28 days)" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60(8) (src:2023)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 60(8) the FCA must give the person notice that it is minded to suspend or cancel (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 60(8) give the person notice that it is minded to suspend or cancel`

-- src:2028 | (9) The FCA must then decide, within a reasonable period, whether to suspend or cancel the person's registration and it must give that person notice of—
-- src:2029 | (a) its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration; or
-- src:2030 | (b) the following matters—
-- src:2031 | (i) its decision to suspend or cancel the person's registration and, subject to paragraph (10), the date from which the suspension or cancellation takes effect;
-- src:2032 | (ii) the period of the suspension;
-- src:2033 | (iii) the reasons for its decision; and
-- src:2034 | (iv) the right to appeal under regulation 93.
@ref reg 60(9) (src:2028-2034)
GIVEN `the FCA has given the notice under paragraph (8) and the period for representations has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the FCA decided within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states its decision to suspend or cancel the registration and the date from which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the period of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the reasons for its decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(9) the FCA has decided and given the person notice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the FCA has given the notice under paragraph (8) and the period for representations has expired`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The FCA must then decide" -- the steps in paragraph (8) have not been taken; an unmet condition (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the FCA decided within a reasonable period`
            AND (`the notice states its decision not to suspend or cancel the person's registration`
                 OR (`the notice states its decision to suspend or cancel the registration and the date from which it takes effect`
                     AND `the notice states the period of the suspension`
                     AND `the notice states the reasons for its decision`
                     AND `the notice states the right to appeal under regulation 93`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must then decide, within a reasonable period, ... and it must give that person notice of" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60(9) (src:2028)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 60(9) the FCA must decide and give the person notice (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 60(9) decide and give the person notice`

-- src:2035 | (10) If the registering authority—
-- src:2036 | (a) considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation of a person's registration to have immediate effect; and
-- src:2037 | (b) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it in the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9),
-- src:2038 | the suspension or cancellation takes effect when the notice is given to the person.
@ref reg 60(10) (src:2035-2038)
GIVEN `the registering authority considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation to have immediate effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(10) the suspension or cancellation takes effect when the notice is given` MEANS
    IF `the registering authority considers that the interests of the public require the suspension or cancellation to have immediate effect`
       AND `the notice given under paragraph (7) or (9) includes a statement to that effect and the reasons for it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the registering authority (a) considers ... and (b) includes a statement ..., the suspension or cancellation takes effect when the notice is given" -- an unmet "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2039 | (11) Where the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person’s registration, the authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish such information about that decision as the authority considers appropriate.
@ref reg 60(11) (src:2039)
GIVEN `the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person's registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(11) the registering authority may publish information about its decision` MEANS
    IF `the registering authority decides to suspend or cancel a person's registration` AND `it considers it proportionate to publish such information about that decision as it considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the registering authority decides ..., the authority may, if it considers it proportionate to do so, publish" -- an unmet "where" or "if" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2040 | (12) Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (11) and the person whose registration is suspended or cancelled refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal, the supervisory authority must, without delay, publish information about the status of the appeal and its outcome in the same manner as that in which the information was published under paragraph (11).
@ref reg 60(12) (src:2040)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person whose registration is suspended or cancelled refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay, in the same manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60(12) the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (11)`) OR (NOT `the person whose registration is suspended or cancelled refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the supervisory authority publishes information under paragraph (11) and the person ... refers the matter to the Upper Tribunal" -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the supervisory authority has published the status of the appeal and its outcome without delay, in the same manner`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, without delay, publish" (Marginal readings, (c))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60(12) (src:2040)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A DEONTIC Authority `reg 53 act of a registering authority`
`reg 60(12) the supervisory authority must publish the status of the appeal (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY authority
    MUST `reg 60(12) publish the status of the appeal and its outcome`

-- SEAM S-19 (answering): regs 93 and 99 ask which decisions can be appealed.
-- src:2017 | (7) Where the Commissioners decide to suspend or cancel a person's registration they must give that person notice of—
@ref reg 60(7) (src:2017)
GIVEN `the decision is to suspend or cancel a registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60 the decision suspends or cancels a registration` MEANS `the decision is to suspend or cancel a registration`

§ `Part 6 Chapter 3 -- Disclosure obligation (regs 60A and 60B)`

§§ `Regulation 60A -- Disclosure by cryptoasset businesses`

-- SEAM S-K1 (asking): whether the cryptoasset business has established a business relationship is
-- reg 4's answer.  Paragraph (2) applies where (a) it does, or enters into a transaction, out of
-- its activities as a cryptoasset business, and (b) the activity is not within the Ombudsman's
-- jurisdiction (i), or not under the Compensation Scheme's protection (ii), or neither (iii).
-- The three limbs are read as three cases, so paragraph (2) applies unless the activity is within
-- both schemes (marginal reading (j), NOTES.md).
-- src:2043 | (1) Paragraph (2) applies where—
-- src:2044 | (a) a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider (“cryptoasset business”) establishes a business relationship, or enters into a transaction, with a customer that arises out of any of its activities as a cryptoasset business, and
-- src:2045 | (b) the activity is not—
-- src:2046 | (i) within scope of the jurisdiction of the Financial Ombudsman Service, or
-- src:2047 | (ii) subject to protection under the Financial Services Compensation Scheme, or
-- src:2048 | (iii) within scope of the jurisdiction of, or subject to protection under, either of the schemes referred to in paragraph (i) or (ii).
@ref reg 60A(1) (src:2043-2048)
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking)
GIVEN `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it enters into a transaction with a customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises out of any of its activities as a cryptoasset business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is within the scope of the jurisdiction of the Financial Ombudsman Service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is subject to protection under the Financial Services Compensation Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60A(1) paragraph (2) applies` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider`) OR (NOT `it arises out of any of its activities as a cryptoasset business`)
       OR (`the activity is within the scope of the jurisdiction of the Financial Ombudsman Service` AND `the activity is subject to protection under the Financial Services Compensation Scheme`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies where (a) ... and (b) the activity is not ..." -- an unmet "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it enters into a transaction with a customer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) applies where (a) ... establishes a business relationship, or enters into a transaction" -- there is neither
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
              -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether there is a business relationship is reg 4's answer and it has not been given
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:2049 | (2) Before establishing the business relationship or entering into the transaction, the cryptoasset business must inform the customer of the position in paragraph (1)(b)(i), (ii) or (iii), as the case may be.
@ref reg 60A(2) (src:2049)
GIVEN `paragraph (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the cryptoasset business informed the customer of the position before establishing the business relationship or entering into the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60A(2) the cryptoasset business has informed the customer before establishing the business relationship or entering into the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph (2) applies`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (2) applies is paragraph (1)'s answer and it has not been given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the cryptoasset business informed the customer of the position before establishing the business relationship or entering into the transaction`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before establishing the business relationship or entering into the transaction, the cryptoasset business must inform the customer" (Marginal readings, (c))
        ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref reg 60A(2) (src:2049)
GIVEN person IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC STRING `reg 56 act of a person`
`reg 60A(2) the cryptoasset business must inform the customer (as an obligation)` MEANS
    PARTY person
    MUST `reg 60A(2) inform the customer`

-- Reg 60A(3) defines the two schemes by pointing at the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000.
-- Whether a given scheme was established under Part 16 (or Part 15) is a fact the person can state;
-- "means" is closed, so a scheme not so established is not the one defined (JUST FALSE).
-- src:2050 | (3) In this regulation—
-- src:2051 | (a) the Financial Ombudsman Service means the scheme established under Part 16 of FSMA ;
@ref reg 60A(3)(a) (src:2050-2051)
GIVEN `the scheme is the scheme established under Part 16 of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60A(3)(a) the scheme is the Financial Ombudsman Service` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is the scheme established under Part 16 of FSMA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Financial Ombudsman Service means the scheme established under Part 16 of FSMA" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:2052 | (b) the Financial Services Compensation Scheme means the scheme established under Part 15 of FSMA .
@ref reg 60A(3)(b) (src:2052)
GIVEN `the scheme is the scheme established under Part 15 of FSMA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60A(3)(b) the scheme is the Financial Services Compensation Scheme` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is the scheme established under Part 15 of FSMA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Financial Services Compensation Scheme means the scheme established under Part 15 of FSMA" -- a closed definition
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 60B -- Changes in control of registered cryptoasset businesses`

-- src:2054 | Schedule 6B applies to an acquisition of or increase in control over a registered cryptoasset business (within the meaning given at regulation 59(8)).
@ref reg 60B (src:2054)
GIVEN `it is an acquisition of or increase in control over a registered cryptoasset business within the meaning given at regulation 59(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 60B Schedule 6B applies to the acquisition or increase in control` MEANS
    IF `it is an acquisition of or increase in control over a registered cryptoasset business within the meaning given at regulation 59(8)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Schedule 6B applies to an acquisition of or increase in control over a registered cryptoasset business" -- another acquisition is outside the regulation
    ELSE NOTHING
